        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1062">

                <pb facs="1108" n="988" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg988"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.01/26: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Edge</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-04-18T10:00:00+00:00">April 18, 1931—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received April 18—9:40 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>180. Department’s 145, April 17, 5 p.m. A communiqué was issued by the Foreign
                    Office last night at 8 o’clock to the effect that the French Government had
                    recognized the Spanish Republic.</p>
                <p>I have confirmed this this morning from the Foreign Office which states that the
                    formal written reply to the note from the Spanish Chargé d’Affaires here (see my
                    telegram number 173, April 17, 1 p.m.<anchor n="5" xml:id="d1062-f1"/>) in which
                    the latter had announced the establishment of the <pb facs="1109" n="989"
                        xml:id="pg989"/> Provisional Government of the Republic in Spain, took note
                    of this fact and added that the French Government accorded its recognition to
                    the new Spanish Government.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edge</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
